<title>USA: Western Country 1996 shr loss widens.</title>
<headline>Western Country 1996 shr loss widens.</headline>
<dateline>OKLAHOMA CITY 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996	    1995</p>
<p> Revenues			     $ 7,667,685   $ 8,508,058</p>
<p> Net profit (loss)		  (1,913,446)     (211,233)</p>
<p>Earnings (losses) per</p>
<p>  common share				(.63)	   (.07)</p>
<p>Weighted average common</p>
<p>  shares outstanding		  3,035,079     3,161,000</p>
<p>NOTE: Company attributed 1996 loss primarily to declining sales at its Tucson club and the asset writedown at the same club, which resulted in a loss of about $2.14 million. The company recently entered into agreements to sell the Tucson club's assets and settle related liabilities, which, when closed, will results in a partial recovery of the losses.</p>
<p>Full company name is Western Country Clubs Inc.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
